Stockholm - the " [:a {:href "/results/70055"} "European (German)"] ", the " [:a {:href "/results/70057"} "Swedish"] ", and a " [:a {:href "/results/70056"} "Free System"] ", with free choice of movements and apparatus.  This would be repeated in " [:a {:href "/editions/7/sports/GAR"} "1920 at Antwerp"] ", when the same three styles were used for three separate team events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Individual gymnastics also had its exponents and its detractors.  In particular, the Swedes did not like the idea of gymnastics as an individual competition, as it was against their basic concept of gymnastics.  In 1908, the Swedish press did not publish the results of the individual gymnastics competition at London, as there were no Swedish participants.  Still, the Swedish Olympic Committee agreed to organize an individual gymnastics event in Stockholm.  In fact, at the 11th IOC Session (1910 in Luxembourg), the Swedish Olympic Committee revealed that they were not planning on conducting any competitive gymnastics, but only displays.  The Swedish Olympic Committee capitulated to the wishes of the " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] " and agreed to organize competitive events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All of the Olympic gymnastics events were held outdoors in the " [:a {:href "/venues/233"} "Olympic Stadium"] ", which was common in that era."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70050"} "Individual All-Around, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "44"] "\n" [:td {} "9"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70055"} "Team All-Around, European System, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "11 July 1912"] "\n" [:td {} "91"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {